# Try the API from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each ### block.
# Start the app first (mvn spring-boot:run). Put your admin password below, but DO NOT commit the real one.

@host = http://localhost:8081
@adminPassword = PASTE_YOUR_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HERE

### 1. Log in as admin (saves the token for the requests below)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 2. List categories
GET {{host}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a product (admin only). categoryId 1 = Electronics from the seed data
# @name createProduct
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "USB-C-1M",
  "name": "USB-C cable 1m",
  "description": "Braided charging cable",
  "price": 6.50,
  "quantity": 3,
  "reorderLevel": 5,
  "categoryId": 1
}

###
@productId = {{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### 4. Search products (text, category, paging, sorting)
GET {{host}}/api/products?q=usb&page=0&size=10&sort=price&dir=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Low stock report
GET {{host}}/api/products/low-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Receive stock (IN)
POST {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/movements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "IN", "quantity": 50, "note": "Supplier delivery" }

### 7. Sell stock (OUT). Asking for more than exists returns 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/movements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "OUT", "quantity": 4, "note": "Sale" }

### 8. Movement history for the product
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/movements?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Register a STAFF user (staff cannot create products: expect 403 later)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "mary.staff", "email": "mary@example.com", "password": "a-long-staff-password" }
